    "description_md": "Cetacean species detections from environmental DNA (eDNA) in seawater samples collected by the NOAA CalCOFI Genomics Program (NCOG) at 10-40 m (a few deeper) on CalCOFI cruises, 2014-2016. Seven dolphin and whale species detected by metabarcoding: 1 = detected, 0 = not detected in a sequenced sample (a non-detection, not a confirmed absence). The 62 samples listed as \"not sequenced, PCR negative\" did not amplify, so they say nothing about any species: each stays a sample with no edna_presence rows (not a 0) until the provider says what a PCR negative means (Q04). Samples have no parent sample (each is a root event); the CalCOFI bottle each was filtered from is matched only as evidence of its time and cruise. Each sample is timed by its CTD-rosette bottle cast. Staged from the CalCOFI marine mammal Shiny app repository (CalCOFI/marmam-app).\n",
    "keywords": ["EARTH SCIENCE > BIOLOGICAL CLASSIFICATION > ANIMALS/VERTEBRATES > MAMMALS", "Marine Turtles, Birds, and Mammals"],
